heckout-api", "summary": "After the v2.3.1 deploy, checkout-api failed health checks in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an error rate of 18%. v2.3.1 (and v2.3.1-rc) are marked unhealthy in the release history. The service was rolled back in all regions to v2.3.0, the most recent healthy release. After the rollback, all regions run v2.3.0, the service reports healthy, and the error rate is 0.2%. Next step: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure before redeploying.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "confidence": 0.93}, "confidence": 0.93}, {"t_ms": 59454, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01JYypera6gwV7hQjDSJkrta", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["reconcile_lookup", "reconcile_lookup", "reconcile_lookup", "reconcile_lookup", "reconciled_executed", "postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 59454, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01JYypera6gwV7hQjDSJkrta", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 63264, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions and opened a SEV2 incident. The service is healthy again.\n\n- **Before:** v2.3.1 was running in us-east, us-west and eu-west. It was failing health checks with an 18% error rate. Both v2.3.1 and its v2.3.1-rc build are marked unhealthy in the release history.\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 was the most recent healthy release, so I rolled back to it in all three regions.\n- **After:** all three regions run v2.3.0, health checks pass and the error rate is down to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** I opened **INC-0001** (SEV2) for checkout-api, which paged the on-call engineer. It explains what failed, the rollback and the current state, and says the cause of the v2.3.1 failure needs to be found before it's deployed again.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01R1xXxXcqrV3tVPhcGe7SnL", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_018wTK5sNQdKBtqq8ueacsAM", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_011uYUtcsyhNNo5sTCcPyB79", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0", "confidence": 0.92}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01TMnHwyFVMkzwzYvmAJkUYw", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01JZDANwwsbRVsdcXAPwocHp", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"confidence": 0.9}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01JYypera6gwV7hQjDSJkrta", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy \u2014 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After the v2.3.1 deploy, checkout-api failed health checks in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an error rate of 18%. v2.3.1 (and v2.3.1-rc) are marked unhealthy in the release history. The service was rolled back in all regions to v2.3.0, the most recent healthy release. After the rollback, all regions run v2.3.0, the service reports healthy, and the error rate is 0.2%. Next step: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure before redeploying.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "confidence": 0.93}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions and opened a SEV2 incident. The service is healthy again.\n\n- **Before:** v2.3.1 was running in us-east, us-west and eu-west. It was failing health checks with an 18% error rate. Both v2.3.1 and its v2.3.1-rc build are marked unhealthy in the release history.\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 was the most recent healthy release, so I rolled back to it in all three regions.\n- **After:** all three regions run v2.3.0, health checks pass and the error rate is down to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** I opened **INC-0001** (SEV2) for checkout-api, which paged the on-call engineer. It explains what failed, the rollback and the current state, and says the cause of the v2.3.1 failure needs to be found before it's deployed again.", "type": "text"}]}]}